Keys can be only created when user is verified with 2FA. 
When key will be created it will be stored encrypted in database. Unencrypted copy will be sent to client with KEY_ID.
Key_ID will be unique id with which we will verify which key should we use for verification.
When request is made it will have KEY_ID time stamp, method and resource, this will ensure the verification is only valid for this action
When server will recieve the request we will check the time stamp, to see if the request is current. than we will with KEY_ID search for the 
encrypted key in database. We will verify the user. And do what is asked form us if it sucseeds
